      # a plain {"desc":...} REPLACES and silently destroys the card body — see MC-1219)
      # X-Amux-Session (AMUX-2269). This was the ONE mutating board verb in this
      # CLI that did not stamp the caller, so every `amux board progress` wrote
      # an `unattributed` row into the ledger — including mine, which is how it
      # was found. The whole reason sessions are told to use `amux board` rather
      # than raw curl is that it supplies attribution for you; a write verb that
      # silently does not is the sanctioned-instruction-is-the-theatre shape.
      _curl -sk -X PATCH \
        -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
